  },
  {
    "insert": "In scientific papers, it is also very important to use appropriate wording and to use high-quality language to ensure clarity, professionalism and credibility. Your exposé contains a few grammatical errors (e.g. \"react\" - \"reacts\") and non-scientific formulations (\"use common sense\"). In addition, scientific papers should be formulated indirectly and objective (this work vs. our work). To improve the linguistic quality of your exposé, consider reading some scientific papers to familiarise yourself with appropriate terminology and academic phrasing. "
